    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5512747/casual-van-driver": {
      "title": "CASUAL Van Driver",
      "description": "CASUAL Van Driver Location UH West O'ahu, Kapolei, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-02180 Department University of Hawai'i - West O'ahu - Student Affairs Opening Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date 10/13/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: CASUAL Description * * * * Applicants seeking short-term or part-time work with the University Hawai'i may apply for Casual Hire positions, which include administrative, professional, and technical (APT) or instructional-type positions. Because of the temporary nature of these appointments, Casual Hire employees are not eligible for most benefits as provided to regular BOR and Civil Service employees. Casual Hire appointments may last for up to 89 days for full-time employees, and up to 1 calendar year for part­time employees. Title: CASUAL Van Driver Hiring Unit: UH West Oahu Student Affairs Position Number: ****Casual Hire Location: Kapolei Date Posted: 10/09/2026 Closing Date: 10/13/2026 Salary: $27.98/hour Work Schedule: Mon – Fri; variable hours Permanent/Temporary: Temporary Full time/Part time: Part time The Van Driver is responsible for the safe and efficient transport of customers in a passenger van. Van Drivers must provide superior customer service experience for each passenger. In this visible role, it is important that the Van Driver maintains a positive attitude and professional appearance at all times. Duties and Responsibilities: Transports passengers in a van between UH-West O’ahu and designated drop-off/pick-up areas. Welcomes each customer with a smile. Provides information, direction and assistance as needed. Treats all passengers in a courteous, friendly and professional manner. Operates a passenger van safely and efficiently. Follows scheduled routes, chartered routes or responds to requests from management for unscheduled pick-ups or drop-offs. Kindly assists passengers in boarding and exiting the vehicle Reports accidents, safety situations, vehicle condition, or any damages to supervisor. Reports items left behind and maintains a log of items. Inspects exterior and interior of vehicle at beginning of each shift for properly operating headlights, turn signals, brake lights, interior lighting, air conditioning, mirror adjustment, properly inflated tires, windshield wipers, etc. prior to driving the van. Ensures that both inside and outside of the vehicle are properly cleaned. Responsible for keeping the van fueled. Maintains orderly conduct of passengers within the vehicle. Accurately completes driver trip sheet each shift with information including number of passengers, user UHID numbers, pick up and drop off times, mileage, destinations, etc. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: A valid driver’s license to drive in the State of Hawaii. One-year work experience in operation of a motorized vehicle. Knowledge and understanding of the method of operating motorized equipment; laws, rules and regulations governing operation of motor vehicle on streets and highways; hazards and safety precautions. Exceptional customer service skills. Strong communication skills, both written and oral. Able to sit for up to 6 hours per shift. Ability to complete log and trip sheets accurately. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively in a courteous manner. Ability to solve problems and make sound decisions. To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Applicant must submit the following: Cover letter indicating interest in the position and how the minimum qualifications of the position are met. Current resume’ References - names and contact information (telephone number and email addresses) of at least three professional references. Note: Late, incomplete, or unreadable application materials will not be considered. Please redact any social security number and/or birth date on your documents prior to submitting. Please create an account if this is your 